{
  "dom_id": "step-17678",
  "name": "Example: \n                    Evaluating Expressions Containing Radicals and One or Two Additional Operations",
  "problem": "What is the value of $7\\times \\sqrt[3]{-8}?$",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. In terms of the order of operations: \n\n- expressions underneath radicals are treated the same as parentheses\n\n- radicals themselves are treated as exponents\n\nTherefore, we first evaluate the value of the radical, and we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7\\times \\sqrt[3]{-8} & = \\\\ 7\\times \\sqrt[3]{(-2)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-2)} & = \\\\ 7\\times \\sqrt[3]{(-2)^{3}} & = \\\\ 7\\times (-2) & = \\\\ -14.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
